# Shell scripts must keep LF on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (this repo's recommended Windows setting) otherwise checks
# these out with CRLF, and bash then fails on the very first line:
#   $'\r': command not found
#   set: usage: ...
# That is not a shell-portability nicety: the Linux gate is the only automated
# proof that the non-Windows build works, and a CRLF checkout makes it abort
# before it can prove anything (observed on 2026-11-03).
*.sh text eol=lf
